    "url": "https://www.weaving.news/news/019cd363-9fef-72bc-9036-3ac5f781360c",
    "title": "Restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX Part 1: PSU and Nvram",
    "snippet": "An article examines the restoration of a Sun SPARCstation IPX, situating it within early-1990s UNIX workstation history, outlining its hardware specifications and SPARC architecture origins, and describing a common failure in IPX/IPC power supplies due to degraded electrolytic capacitors, with notes on repair references.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://justanotherelectronicsblog.com/?p=1305",
    "title": "Restoring a SUN SPARCstation IPX lunchbox computer",
    "snippet": "The Sun SPARCstation IPX in this photo was send to me by a friend to repair, as it didn’t output anything on a monitor. So let’s have a peek inside, see how to repair it and take a look at what kind of maintenance a computer from 1991 needs!   Summarize",
    "published": null
