    "url": "https://www.hazumi.news/posts/47310296",
    "title": "Restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX Part 1: PSU and Nvram",
    "snippet": "This article explores the process of restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX, focusing on the power supply unit (PSU) and non-volatile RAM (NVRAM) components. It provides step-by-step instructions and insights into the diagnostic and repair procedures involved in reviving this vintage workstation.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPARCstation_IPX",
    "title": "SPARCstation IPX - Wikipedia",
    "snippet": "Aug 22, 2015         The successor to the SPARCstation IPC, Sun introduced the SPARCstation IPX on July 22, 1991. It is based on the sun4c architecture, and is enclosed in a lunchbox chassis. Intended as a mid-range offering in their SPARCstation line of workstations, the SPARCstation IPX sold for US$11,995 at the low end and US$13,495 at the high end.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://hb.int2inf.com/s/item/QP5AMrKjbneVv7csN7KJoQ-restoring-sun-sparcstation-ipx-part1",
    "title": "Restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX Part 1: PSU and Nvram | Hasty Briefs",
    "snippet": "The SPARCstation IPX featured a 40MHz SPARC CPU, up to 64MB RAM, and specialized hardware for multitasking and UNIX performance. Common issues with the SPARCstation IPX include failed electrolytic capacitors in the power supply, often due to aging or poor-quality components.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://blog.adafruit.com/2026/03/10/restoring-a-sun-sparcstation-ipx/",
    "title": "Restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX - Adafruit Industries",
    "snippet": "Mar 10, 2026         Restoring a Sun SPARCstation IPX Andrew Back posts about restoring a vintage Sun SPARCstation IPX workstation. If you worked in computing in the early 1990s, studied computer science around then, or just had a keen interest in computers, the chances are that Sun Microsystems was a familiar name and their workstations were highly coveted.",
    "published": null
